        "id": "ch16_2_4-1",
        "text": "Classes\nA class is a logical definition of an object that defines the properties and methods of the object \u2013 a\nrecipe. It is an implementation of a type. Back in Chapter 4 , PowerShell Variables and Data Structures ,\nwe created three objects of type Imaginary.Bike ,  by creating the objects and their properties\nand labeling them as Imaginary.Bike . We could also have defined a class of objects called\nImaginary.Bike with the same properties and methods, using a constructor to create actual\ninstances of the class. We use classes when we want to be able to create objects easily and repeatably.",
